      "writtenOn": "2017-01-16T21:12:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got it - I see what you mean. Creating groups on-the-fly would pose the same issue as creating role assignments. As far as your question goes I would assume that we have that ability now that we have a shadow user implementation. But, in digging through the code I can\u0027t seem to find where we explicitly add shadow users to groups from the mapping. This is confusing since the GET /v3/auth/projects API will return projects that user has access to via a group.\n\nLooking at the implementation of both the Mapped plugin and the GET /v3/auth/projects API makes it clear that we don\u0027t determine the groups a user is a member of from the user_id. Instead the Mapped plugin overrides the user_id and group_ids variables of the auth_context, which seem to be pulled out later and used in GET /v3/auth/projects.\n\nI think this case should be handled as a backwards compatibility fix for shadow users. The Mapped plugin never really took users into account since they were ephemeral. Now that we actually have a reference, we can check the group IDs and build the list of projects a user has access to based on the user id (which now points to a shadow user) and a list of groups that shadow user might be in.",
      "parentUuid": "7a3c09a3_c77be426",
      "revId": "617a3d95eabcfac21e1419fc0ca5904e832315a3",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
